---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Shell & CLI | ORASOLU"
  description="Practical command-line workflows for Oracle administration, Linux operations and repeatable troubleshooting."
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · AUTOMATION &amp; DEVOPS</div>
        <h1>Shell & CLI</h1>
        <p>
          Practical command-line workflows for Oracle administration, Linux operations and repeatable troubleshooting.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · AUTOMATION &amp; DEVOPS</div>
          <h2>Use the command line to make routine work repeatable</h2>
          <p>
            Shell and CLI workflows are useful when database administration involves repeated checks, file handling and operational tasks. These examples provide practical starting points for repeatable Oracle and Linux administration.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">01 · DATABASE</div>
              <h2>Check Oracle environment</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review the Oracle environment variables and client context used by a shell session.
            </p>
            <pre><code>printf 'ORACLE_SID=%s\nORACLE_HOME=%s\nPATH=%s\n' "$ORACLE_SID" "$ORACLE_HOME" "$PATH"</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">02 · INSTANCE</div>
              <h2>Check database instance</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Confirm the instance name and status from a command-line SQL session.
            </p>
            <pre><code>sqlplus -s / as sysdba &lt;&lt;'SQL'
SET PAGESIZE 0 FEEDBACK OFF VERIFY OFF HEADING OFF
SELECT instance_name || ' ' || status
FROM v$instance;
EXIT
SQL</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">03 · STORAGE</div>
              <h2>Check filesystem usage</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review filesystem capacity before database files or backups consume available space.
            </p>
            <pre><code>df -h
printf '\nFilesystem usage above 80%%:\n'
df -P | awk 'NR &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; $5+0 &gt;= 80 &#123;print&#125;'</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">04 · PROCESSES</div>
              <h2>Review Oracle processes</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review Oracle-related processes from the operating system when investigating instance activity.
            </p>
            <pre><code>ps -ef | grep '[o]ra_' | sort</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">05 · LOGGING</div>
              <h2>Capture command output</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Capture command output to a timestamped log for repeatable operational evidence.
            </p>
            <pre><code>LOG_DIR=/tmp/oracle_checks
mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR"
LOG_FILE="$LOG_DIR/check_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S).log"

&#123;
  date
  hostname
  id
  df -h
&#125; | tee "$LOG_FILE" </code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">06 · SCRIPTING</div>
              <h2>Run a repeatable check</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Use a small shell function to standardize a frequently repeated database check.
            </p>
            <pre><code>check_instance() &#123;
  sqlplus -s / as sysdba &lt;&lt;'SQL'
SET PAGESIZE 0 FEEDBACK OFF HEADING OFF
SELECT instance_name || ' ' || status
FROM v$instance;
EXIT
SQL
&#125;

check_instance</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <div class="resource-note__label">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · AUTOMATION &amp; DEVOPS</div>
          <h3>Good automation starts with a repeatable command.</h3>
          <p>
            Use command-line checks to establish a known workflow, then add validation and logging before turning the process into scheduled or unattended automation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/automation/">
            Back to Automation &amp; DevOps
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";

    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>

<style>
.resource-section {
  padding-top: 56px;
  padding-bottom: 72px;
}

.resource-intro {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}

.resource-intro h2 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.resource-intro p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.resource-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 22px;
  align-items: start;
}

.resource-block {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  height: 560px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 30px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: #ffffff;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  transition:
    border-color 0.22s ease,
    box-shadow 0.22s ease,
    transform 0.22s ease;
}

.resource-block:hover {
  border-color: #d8dce1;
  box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
  transform: translateY(-3px);
}

.resource-block__header {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.resource-block__label {
  margin-bottom: 9px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.2;
}

.resource-block h2 {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.resource-block__description {
  min-height: 48px;
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}

.resource-block pre {
  position: relative;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 22px;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overflow-y: auto;
  background: #2f353d;
  border-radius: 10px;
  color: #f3f4f6;
  font-family:
    "Cascadia Code",
    "Consolas",
    "Courier New",
    monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.7;
  white-space: pre;
}

.resource-block code {
  font-family: inherit;
  white-space: pre;
}

.resource-copy-button {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  right: 10px;
  padding: 5px 9px;
  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #374151;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  cursor: pointer;
  z-index: 2;
}

.resource-copy-button:hover {
  background: #f3f4f6;
}

.resource-note {
  margin-top: 32px;
  padding: 30px;
  background: #f7f8fa;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
}

.resource-note__label {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
}

.resource-note h3 {
  margin: 0 0 12px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.resource-note p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.resource-actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 24px;
  margin-top: 32px;
}

@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 680px) {
  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 52px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .resource-block {
    height: 520px;
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 0;
  }

  .resource-block pre {
    padding: 18px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .resource-note {
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .resource-actions {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 18px;
  }
}
</style>
